+## Symlinks
+
+Symbolic links stored in `zip` and `squashfs` archives are skipped by
+default. Use `-l`/`--links` to expose them as regular files with a
+`.rclonelink` suffix, in the same way as the local backend does.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+```
+
+The size of a `.rclonelink` object is the length of the link target,
+and reading it returns the target path. This means copying with
+`--links` recreates the symlinks on a destination which supports them.
+
+```
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular archive member whose name ends in `.rclonelink` is still
+treated as a regular file.
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
